      "measure.perimeter": "Literal uint8 casting, source coefficient construction and scalar boxing remain explicit providers. Binary erosion, byte border subtraction, modulo-256 stencil counts and the 50-term sum are owned C++. Default cases use the existing seed 2026 gray image thresholded above 127 for uint8 or above 0.5 for floats, then cast back to the same dtype: binary masks with roughly half the pixels foreground, not arbitrary labels. Mask construction stays outside timing; public casting, allocation, erosion, counts and sum stay inside. The frozen exact-rational 2*gamma_100*S checker runs outside timing."
